prs.body:
- Fixes JSX text holding \u{ swallowing the expression container after it, e.g. \u{1} as an element's children lexed as one text token instead of text, {, 1, }
- Fixes identifier escape scans running through NBSP and other Unicode whitespace, e.g. thisA in a\u{41} in this\u{41} (NBSP separated) lexed as the keyword this
- No token changes on the conformance suites or local corpora, perf neutral

Stacked labels on a loop are all valid `continue` targets. Named continues to outer labels currently lose their CFG jump edges, causing false positives in `no-unreachable` and `no-unreachable-loop`:

```js
function count() {
  let n = 0;
  a: b: do { n++; continue a; } while (n < 3);
  return n;
}
```

Queue named continues in the loop context immediately after their matched label stack, preserving unlabeled continue lookup and distinct labeled break targets. Resolve `do…while` continue edges before its condition's outgoing edges so the exit inherits the condition's reachable state. Regression tests cover all five loop forms, every position in a three-label stack, nested continues, and `do…while` exit reachability.

ESLint 10.14.0 currently shares the reported false positives; the issue's examples both return `3` in Node.

Fixes #28945
